# NOTE ON WHAT IS IGNORED HERE. This repository is shared through GitHub, so
# anything not committed does not exist on the other one. What remains ignored below is
# only output that is regenerated by a documented command from inputs that ARE committed
# (baked packs from data/rom via the bakery, the playable/ test folder from a build).
# Authored work is never ignored, whatever directory it happens to live in.
#
# Build products. Regenerated every build from data/ by the bake tools, and kept out of
# history so the repo does not grow ~23 MB per build; playable builds are published as
# GitHub Releases instead.
#
# NOTE: data/rom and data/dosdata (the cartridge dump and the 1995 CD) ARE committed
# while this repository is private. See DATA.md before making it public.
*.dSYM/
*.dylib
*.log
*.o
*.pyc
*.wav
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
build-native/
build/
# Any cmake output directory, whatever it is called. build-native/ and build/ were
# named individually, so a directory called build-audit/ matched neither and 302
# files of CMake output -- with absolute paths baked into CMakeCache.txt -- were
# committed and then blocked every push from every branch. Match the family.
build-audit/
build-*/
data/dist-*/
data/extracted/
playable/
shots/

# The binaries themselves, by name. Every one of these is a build product.
# app/cnc3d was committed by accident once (383 KB of Mach-O in history); if it is
# still tracked, `git rm --cached app/cnc3d` before the next push, because the
# pre-push hook exists to refuse exactly this.
cnc3d
cnc_eyes
preview
# The standalone pause-dialog layout gate. game/build.sh rebuilds it from
# game/gate_optlayout.c, which IS tracked; the binary is a product like every other here.
game/gate_optlayout
audio/audtest
audio/banktest
audio/mixtest
audio/playtest
video/playvqa
app/cnc3d
input/inputtest
video/playvqa
audio/banktest
audio/audtest
menu/preview
# The bakery's output dir and its cached bytecode; the harness itself is tracked.
#
# bake_pk4.pyc is INCLUDED, and until now it only SAID so. The blanket *.pyc rule above
# matched it and there was no negation, so the one file whose source no longer exists was
# ignored by the rule and present only on machines that already happened to have it. A
# clean checkout could not bake a pack at all, and a lost working copy would have taken
# the only surviving form of that code with it. The negation below is what the comment
# has been claiming since it was written.
tools/bakery/game/
tools/bakery/**/__pycache__/
!tools/bakery/sharecopy/eyes/bake_pk4.pyc

# n64_terrain.py's per-scenario intermediates. Regenerated from the ROM in about four
# minutes for all 36 missions, and 96 MB if committed -- the same rule DATA.md applies
# to baked packs. Proven regenerable byte for byte: re-running the tool reproduces the
# already-tracked SCG01EA/SCB01EA/SCG02EA files with zero differing cells.
# Files already in history stay tracked; this only stops new ones being added.
tools/bakery/sharecopy/assets/terrain/terrain_*.json
tools/bakery/sharecopy/assets/terrain/terrain_*.png
game/*.o.tmp

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO MACHINES, ONE REPO
#
# This project is worked from a Mac and a Windows machine and GitHub is the only
# thing between them, so ANY work that lives only in a working copy is work that can
# be lost. What is ignored below is therefore limited to things that are REGENERATED
# by a command in this repo, and nothing else. If you are about to add a line here,
# ask whether the file can be rebuilt; if it cannot, it is source and it gets
# committed however awkward it looks.
#
# brain/vanilla/ used to be ignored, on the grounds that patches/vanilla-cnc3d.patch
# was the record of everything we change in it. It is not committed as a theory any
# more: on 18 Aug the working checkout was found to have drifted AHEAD of its own
# patch, CI was failing on every push because of it, and it went unnoticed.
# The checkout itself is now the record. Its build-native/ stays ignored, being a
# build directory.

# The build number header, written by tools/version.sh before every compile.
game/cnc3d_build.h

# The launcher's two build products.
#
# lcfg.h carries the UPDATE HOST AND ITS KEY. The release zips hold data baked from
# the cartridge and the 1995 discs, so the host that serves them is private and
# checks a key, and a key committed here would be a key in every clone and in the
# eventual public export. It is written by tools/launcher/make-config.sh on every
# launcher build, from ~/.cnc3d-update, which lives outside this repo. A machine
# without that file still builds a launcher; it simply says UPDATES OFF.
#
# cnc3d-launcher is a binary like cnc3d and cnc_eyes above. C&C3D.app's script is
# tracked and execs it; the binary is a product.
launcher/lcfg.h
launcher/cnc3d-launcher

# The build's own content stamp. GENERATED by game/build.sh on every build and read by
# playable/Editor.app to warn when the binary predates the source. It was briefly tracked,
# which made it conflict (add/add) on every single merge between two branches that had
# both been built -- which is every merge. It is a build artifact and belongs here.
game/.build-sources.sha
brain/xl/build-native/
brain/xl/build-win/
